{"qid":"Q79","names":["Republic of Egypt","Arab Republic of Egypt"],"title":"Republic of Egypt","endonym":{"native":"Egypt","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The Republic of Egypt was proclaimed on 18 June 1953, formally ending the Muhammad Ali dynasty's monarchy a year after the Free Officers' coup of July 1952 deposed King Farouk. Muhammad Naguib served as the first president, but was sidelined and forced out in 1954 by Gamal Abdel Nasser, who became the dominant figure and was formally elected president in 1956. Nasser nationalized the Suez Canal Company in July 1956, triggering the Suez Crisis in which an Anglo-French-Israeli invasion was repulsed diplomatically by US and Soviet pressure, cementing his stature as a pan-Arab leader. The republic ended on 22 February 1958 when Egypt merged with Syria to form the United Arab Republic.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Egypt's internationally recognized borders are precisely defined; the dataset's representation reflects the post-1973 return of Sinai and is well attested by treaty and administrative records.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":"place/Egypt","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Egypt","rulers":[{"qid":"Q104392","name":"Mohamed Naguib","start":1953,"end":1954,"image":"Mohamed Naguib1952.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mohamed%20Naguib1952.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Ashkroft Bombai","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q39524","name":"Gamal Abdel Nasser","start":1956,"end":1970,"image":"Official Portrait - Gamal Abdel Nasser.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/S